# surfaceflinger on this device additionally serves on /dev/vndbinder
# (ro.vendor.sf.vndbinder + tools/patches/surfaceflinger-publish-vndbinder.patch;
# decode lane 2026-08-15, VENC_LANE.md): the MTK GuiExt pool inside
# composer@2.1-service resolves "SurfaceFlinger" there before handing
# MtkOmxVdec its surface output buffers.
#
# A coredomain touching vndbinder_device/vndservice_manager_type collides with
# the full_treble_only() neverallows in system/sepolicy/public/domain.te.
#
# CORRECTION 2026-09-09 (enforcing lane; the claim below was inherited from the
# LOS16 port, where it was true, and is FALSE on 18.1). This file used to say
# the rules were legal because the device builds with
# PRODUCT_FULL_TREBLE_OVERRIDE := false "(lineage_m95.mk)". There is no such
# assignment in lineage_m95.mk at all -- line 26 there is a VoLTE comment --
# and BoardConfig.mk:113 sets PRODUCT_FULL_TREBLE_OVERRIDE := true.
#
# Measured, not argued: the neverallows ARE in the compiled policy --
# `grep -c "(neverallow ... vndbinder_device"` over
# out/.../system/etc/selinux/plat_sepolicy.cil gives 14, and 10 for
# vndservice_manager_type. Which is exactly why both rules below stay dropped:
# there is no exempting attribute for a coredomain on vndbinder, so this is not
# "forward hygiene pending a boot" -- it is a road that is closed. See
# SELINUX_ENFORCING_PLAN.md corner (в3).
# R-SPLIT-DROP (vndbinder mirror off): vndbinder_use(surfaceflinger)
# R-SPLIT-DROP (R neverallow, permissive covers; re-add from denials): allow surfaceflinger surfaceflinger_vndservice:service_manager add;

# The composer process is the observed vndbinder-side consumer
# (BpServiceManager::getService loop in Binder:378_2, capture venc_stk378.txt).
# Its binder_call to surfaceflinger is already covered by the platform
# hal_graphics_composer client/server attribute rules.
allow hal_graphics_composer_default surfaceflinger_vndservice:service_manager find;
